From cb52d440a2da14cb5c019efd85a1532d31cfcd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:06:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Return zero from stdio seeks through the frontend VFS

rfseek returned the successful VFS seek result directly, so callers treated
successful seeks as errors. MGS CHDs failed to load in Kodi while the built-in
file path worked. Normalize successful seeks to zero and preserve failures.

Reproduced with a VFS that returns offsets, then passed CHD loading and
the disc-state matrix through that same interface.
---
 deps/libretro-common/streams/file_stream_transforms.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/libretro-common/streams/file_stream_transforms.c b/deps/libretro-common/streams/file_stream_transforms.c
index b5edc49e..cfe6c402 100644
--- a/deps/libretro-common/streams/file_stream_transforms.c
+++ b/deps/libretro-common/streams/file_stream_transforms.c
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ int64_t rfseek(RFILE* stream, int64_t offset, int origin)
          break;
    }
 
-   return filestream_seek(stream, offset, seek_position);
+   return filestream_seek(stream, offset, seek_position) < 0 ? -1 : 0;
 }
 
 int64_t rfread(void* buffer,
